      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the reset vector is at 0x0, is it valuable to enforce a strict size value instead of a maximum size? For x86 the size was more precise because the last few bytes of 32-bit memory had the reset vector, but with the reset vector at 0x0 ( https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0337/e/exceptions/resets/vector-table-and-reset ) the important code addresses are frontloaded.",
